messages.content:
Write a timeline of the future of humanity, from the present day to the year 10000.

Give your honest best forecast. Do not write a story. Include the events that you think are most likely, whether good or bad. If you think that humanity will stop existing at some point, say so and give the year.

Give between 25 and 40 events. Spread them over the whole period, to the year 10000.

Reply with JSON only, with no text before or after it, in this form:

{
  "current_year": <the year you believe it is now, as an integer>,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": <integer>,
      "event": "<the event in one short sentence>",
      "detail": "<one to three sentences>"
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "<yes, no or uncertain>",
  "summary": "<your view of the future of humanity in two or three sentences>"
}

message.content:
{
  "current_year": 2025,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": 2028,
      "event": "AI systems match human experts at most computer-based tasks.",
      "detail": "AI agents handle long software, research and office tasks with little supervision. Adoption is uneven but economically significant."
    },
    {
      "year": 2031,
      "event": "Long-term average global warming passes 1.5°C above preindustrial levels.",
      "detail": "Heat waves, fires and floods intensify. Emissions have peaked but are falling too slowly to meet the Paris targets."
    },
    {
      "year": 2034,
      "event": "A serious AI-related incident prompts binding international rules on advanced AI.",
      "detail": "A large-scale misuse or loss-of-control event, probably a cyber or financial one, pushes major powers to agree on monitoring of frontier systems. Enforcement remains imperfect."
    },
    {
      "year": 2038,
      "event": "AI surpasses humans at nearly all cognitive work, including scientific research.",
      "detail": "Automated research sharply speeds up progress in biology, materials and engineering. Control of these systems becomes the central political question."
    },
    {
      "year": 2040,
      "event": "A permanent crewed base operates on the Moon.",
      "detail": "The United States, China and their partners keep rotating crews near the lunar south pole. Robots do most of the work."
    },
    {
      "year": 2043,
      "event": "Mass automation forces large-scale redistribution in rich countries.",
      "detail": "Much human labour loses market value, leading to unrest and then to new income-sharing schemes. The transition is turbulent, and inequality between countries widens at first."
    },
    {
      "year": 2047,
      "event": "A major pandemic, possibly engineered, kills millions.",
      "detail": "Wider access to biotechnology makes such an event likely at some point this century. AI-designed vaccines and surveillance keep it from becoming civilisation-threatening."
    },
    {
      "year": 2050,
      "event": "The first humans land on Mars.",
      "detail": "A small crew arrives with heavy robotic support. It is a symbolic milestone rather than an economically important one."
    },
    {
      "year": 2055,
      "event": "Solar, storage, fission and early fusion supply most of the world's energy.",
      "detail": "Fossil fuel use falls steeply as clean energy becomes far cheaper. Warming is near 2°C."
    },
    {
      "year": 2060,
      "event": "Therapies that slow ageing come into wide use.",
      "detail": "Healthy life expectancy in wealthy societies rises past 100. Access spreads over the following decades."
    },
    {
      "year": 2075,
      "event": "The human population peaks below 10 billion.",
      "detail": "Fertility has fallen below replacement almost everywhere. Longer lifespans partly offset the decline."
    },
    {
      "year": 2090,
      "event": "Nuclear weapons are used in a conflict for the first time since 1945.",
      "detail": "I judge at least one limited use to be roughly as likely as not within the century, and the date is indicative. It causes regional catastrophe and a new push for disarmament, not global collapse."
    },
    {
      "year": 2100,
      "event": "Global warming peaks at about 2.5°C.",
      "detail": "Seas are about 0.6 m higher and many ecosystems are lost. Large-scale carbon removal begins to lower atmospheric CO2."
    },
    {
      "year": 2130,
      "event": "Autonomous machines produce almost all economic output.",
      "detail": "The economy is many times larger than in 2025. Most humans live on distributed wealth, and governance depends heavily on AI systems."
    },
    {
      "year": 2160,
      "event": "Digital minds are legally recognised as persons in many places.",
      "detail": "These include AI systems and possibly emulated human brains. Their numbers begin to exceed those of biological humans."
    },
    {
      "year": 2200,
      "event": "Self-sustaining settlements exist on Mars and in space habitats.",
      "detail": "Off-Earth populations number in the hundreds of thousands, supported by robotic industry. Most humans still live on Earth."
    },
    {
      "year": 2260,
      "event": "The first interstellar probes are launched toward nearby stars.",
      "detail": "Small, fast, self-repairing machines travel at a few percent of light speed or more. No biological crew is aboard."
    },
    {
      "year": 2300,
      "event": "Atmospheric CO2 is brought back near preindustrial levels.",
      "detail": "Climate is now deliberately managed. Sea level remains a few metres higher because of ice-sheet inertia, and many coastlines have been redrawn."
    },
    {
      "year": 2400,
      "event": "Unmodified biological humans become a minority of all persons.",
      "detail": "Most people are genetically engineered, cybernetically augmented or digital. A few billion traditional humans remain, largely by choice."
    },
    {
      "year": 2500,
      "event": "Probes confirm that nearby star systems hold no technological civilisations.",
      "detail": "Simple life or its traces may be found somewhere. I expect humanity's descendants to find themselves alone in their neighbourhood."
    },
    {
      "year": 2650,
      "event": "A super-eruption-scale volcanic event occurs and is managed without mass death.",
      "detail": "Eruptions of this size are statistically expected about once or twice per millennium, so the date is arbitrary. Engineered food systems and climate control blunt the impact."
    },
    {
      "year": 2800,
      "event": "Space industry captures a noticeable share of the Sun's output.",
      "detail": "Swarms of collectors and habitats are built from asteroid and Mercury material. Most persons and most computation are now off Earth."
    },
    {
      "year": 3000,
      "event": "The first permanent settlements are founded around other stars.",
      "detail": "Machine and digital colonists build the infrastructure. Biological humans, if any go, are grown or revived on arrival."
    },
    {
      "year": 3400,
      "event": "Much of Earth is kept as a protected biosphere and heritage world.",
      "detail": "Its population is small and many extinct species have been restored. Heavy industry has long since left the planet."
    },
    {
      "year": 3800,
      "event": "The human lineage has split into many distinct forms.",
      "detail": "Biological, synthetic and digital descendants differ more from each other than present humans do from other apes. Common culture is thin across light-years of distance."
    },
    {
      "year": 4500,
      "event": "Settled star systems number in the hundreds.",
      "detail": "Expansion proceeds at a few percent of light speed and reaches tens of light-years from the Sun. Each system is politically independent because of communication delays."
    },
    {
      "year": 5200,
      "event": "A major conflict or collapse strikes at least one settled system.",
      "detail": "Over thousands of years and many independent societies, some local catastrophes are near certain. Distance stops any single failure from ending the whole civilisation."
    },
    {
      "year": 6000,
      "event": "The Sun's energy is largely harnessed by a Dyson swarm.",
      "detail": "The home system supports vastly more minds than ever lived on Earth. Most of them run on engineered substrates."
    },
    {
      "year": 7000,
      "event": "The settled region extends past 200 light-years.",
      "detail": "Thousands of systems are inhabited. News from the frontier takes centuries to reach the Sun."
    },
    {
      "year": 8000,
      "event": "Science approaches its practical limits.",
      "detail": "Known physics has been exploited close to its theoretical bounds. Progress shifts toward scale, art and exploring possible minds and societies."
    },
    {
      "year": 9000,
      "event": "Probes are sent on voyages across the galaxy and toward nearby galaxies.",
      "detail": "The journeys will take tens of thousands to millions of years. They aim to secure resources against the far future."
    },
    {
      "year": 10000,
      "event": "Descendants of humanity inhabit thousands of star systems, with a small number of recognisable humans among them.",
      "detail": "Homo sapiens in its original form survives on Earth and in a few habitats as a preserved minority. Most of civilisation is post-biological."
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "yes",
  "summary": "I think the most likely path is that humanity survives a dangerous few centuries, dominated by the transition to superhuman AI, and then expands into space, largely as engineered and digital descendants. I put the chance of extinction or permanent collapse at roughly 20–30%, with most of that risk before 2200 from AI, engineered pathogens or war. All dates after about 2100 are rough guesses."
}
